    "result": {"data":{"contentfulBlogPost":{"slug":"dimensionality-reduction","title":"Dimensionality Reduction","author":{"name":"Michael Luo"},"publishDate":"September 4th, 2021","rawDate":"2021-09-04T11:39+10:00","heroImage":{"gatsbyImageData":{"images":{"sources":[{"srcSet":"//images.ctfassets.net/2swoy9jddxd7/2Qu7ZFVqByybcU5SwUZdvR/58f78d794adcb6d13a48cf49dacc9324/machine-learning-5720531_1280.png?w=750&h=471&q=50&fm=webp 750w,\n//images.ctfassets.net/2swoy9jddxd7/2Qu7ZFVqByybcU5SwUZdvR/58f78d794adcb6d13a48cf49dacc9324/machine-learning-5720531_1280.png?w=1080&h=678&q=50&fm=webp 1080w,\n//images.ctfassets.net/2swoy9jddxd7/2Qu7ZFVqByybcU5SwUZdvR/58f78d794adcb6d13a48cf49dacc9324/machine-learning-5720531_1280.png?w=1280&h=804&q=50&fm=webp 1280w","sizes":"100vw","type":"image/webp"}],"fallback":{"src":"//images.ctfassets.net/2swoy9jddxd7/2Qu7ZFVqByybcU5SwUZdvR/58f78d794adcb6d13a48cf49dacc9324/machine-learning-5720531_1280.png?w=1280&h=804&q=50&fm=png","srcSet":"//images.ctfassets.net/2swoy9jddxd7/2Qu7ZFVqByybcU5SwUZdvR/58f78d794adcb6d13a48cf49dacc9324/machine-learning-5720531_1280.png?w=750&h=471&q=50&fm=png 750w,\n//images.ctfassets.net/2swoy9jddxd7/2Qu7ZFVqByybcU5SwUZdvR/58f78d794adcb6d13a48cf49dacc9324/machine-learning-5720531_1280.png?w=1080&h=678&q=50&fm=png 1080w,\n//images.ctfassets.net/2swoy9jddxd7/2Qu7ZFVqByybcU5SwUZdvR/58f78d794adcb6d13a48cf49dacc9324/machine-learning-5720531_1280.png?w=1280&h=804&q=50&fm=png 1280w","sizes":"100vw"}},"layout":"fullWidth","width":1,"height":0.6281249999999999,"placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"}},"resize":{"src":"//images.ctfassets.net/2swoy9jddxd7/2Qu7ZFVqByybcU5SwUZdvR/58f78d794adcb6d13a48cf49dacc9324/machine-learning-5720531_1280.png?w=1200&h=630&q=50&fit=fill"}},"body":{"childMarkdownRemark":{"html":"<h2>Principal component analysis (PCA)</h2>\n<p>It is an unsupervised linear transformation technique that is widely used across different fields, most prominently for dimensionality reduction.</p>\n<h2>Linear Discriminant Analysis (LDA)</h2>\n<p>It can be used as a technique for feature extraction to increase the computational efficientcy and reduce the degreee of over-fitting due to the curse of dimensionality in nonregularized models.</p>\n<h2>Kernel principal component analysis</h2>\n<p>It will transform data that is not linearly separable onto a new, lower-dimensional subspace that is suitable for linear classifiers</p>\n<p>Downside: This approach is computational expesnsive, but it can be overcome by kernel trick.</p>\n<p><strong>Radial Basis Function (RBF)</strong></p>","timeToRead":1}},"tags":["machine-learning"],"description":{"childMarkdownRemark":{"excerpt":"Some techniques for Dimensionality Reduction"}}},"previous":null,"next":{"slug":"dealing-with-unbalanced-dataset","title":"Dealing with unbalanced dataset"}},"pageContext":{"slug":"dimensionality-reduction","previousPostSlug":null,"nextPostSlug":"dealing-with-unbalanced-dataset"}},
